<title>NORWAY: Oil output remains reduced at Statoil's Yme field.</title>
<headline>Oil output remains reduced at Statoil's Yme field.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oil production at the North Sea Yme development continues to run at about 34,000 barrels per day (bpd) against a planned plateau of 50,000 bpd due to problems at two gas compressors, operator Den norske stats oljeselskap AS (Statoil) said on Thursday.</p>
<p>But an upgrade of the gas plant at Yme should be completed by next week, Statoil said in its Status Weekly newsletter.</p>
<p>The compressors pump associated gas back into the reservoir and the technical problems have led to gas being flared instead of reinjected, it said.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
